WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.290
The Rise of Skywalker is filled with plot
twists and references that only older fans

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:08.770
will get — as well as some disturbing ideas
that only mature viewers will notice. Children

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.900
will enjoy the Skywalker Saga's finale just
fine, but will they pick up on these plot

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.360
points? We think not. Spoilers ahead.

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:21.120
So, let's talk about The Rise of Skywalker's
big secret. Rey is Palpatine's granddaughter.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:26.721
Surprise? Eh, maybe not. Abrams has been hinting
that he undid The Last Jedi's "nobody" twist

00:00:26.721 --> 00:00:30.880
for a while now, and leaks about Rey's true
heritage have been circulating on the internet

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:31.460
for months.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.030
But if Palpatine has a granddaughter, that
means he has a kid. If you're old enough to

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.510
know the story of the birds and the bees,
you know that means old, wrinkly, yellow-eyed

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:44.480
Palpatine played a little ding dong ping pong
with some lucky lady. He's fully operational,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.460
if you catch our drift.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.140
“Ha.”

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.480
Unfortunately, The Rise of Skywalker doesn't
reveal the identity of Palpatine's lover or

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:57.350
his children, leaving the comics and novels
to explain those mysteries. That's too bad,

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:01.261
because we'd love to meet the woman who got
seduced by those shapeless black robes. We

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:03.660
bet she has some interesting stories to tell.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:09.700
It took 11 movies, but there's finally a canonically
same-sex couple onscreen in a Star Wars movie.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:14.710
No, it's not the sequel trilogy's most dynamic
couple, Finn and Poe Dameron. It's Commander

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:19.080
D'Acy, one of the top-ranking Resistance officers,
and her wife, a Resistance fighter named Wrobie

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:23.270
Tyce who lock lips while the Resistance is
celebrating the defeat of Palpatine.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:27.490
Kids probably won't even notice the moment,
which is over almost as soon as it begins,

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:31.230
but adults will certainly realize what the
inclusion of a same-sex couple in a Star Wars

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:36.210
feature film means. Over the past four decades,
Star Wars has been remarkably conservative

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.840
when it comes to depicting relationships.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:42.670
But most adults will also realize that it's
a very small step. Simply showing two women

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:47.409
kissing isn't real representation. D'Acy isn't
a real character in the film. We don't know

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:51.830
her hopes, dreams, motivations, or fears.
Heck, we barely even know what she sounds

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:56.100
like. D'Acy was a good start, but Disney and
Lucasfilm still have a long way to go.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.740
Even if children are aware of Carrie Fisher's
passing, they're probably not going to give

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:04.770
too much thought to how Leia returns for The
Rise of Skywalker. There's too much else going

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:09.349
on. For those of us who grew up with Princess
Leia, however, it's almost impossible not

00:02:09.349 --> 00:02:14.760
to think about Fisher's death in 2016 every
time her most famous creation shows up onscreen.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.049
As such, adults are probably going to notice
all the tricks that J. J. Abrams and the Rise

00:02:19.049 --> 00:02:24.359
of Skywalker crew used to give Leia the sendoff
she deserves. As promised, Abrams used outtakes

00:02:24.359 --> 00:02:29.610
from The Force Awakens and The Last Jedi in
Leia's scenes, not a digital recreation. You

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:34.260
can tell. Leia's lines are noticeably vague.
It's up to her scene partners to deliver the

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:34.820
specifics.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:39.659
Given the situation, it actually works pretty
well. Leia is the heart of this movie, and

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:43.519
it's wonderful to get a chance to say goodbye
but the sleight of hand is something most

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.180
adults will definitely notice.

00:02:46.249 --> 00:02:50.819
C-3PO gets The Rise of Skywalker's best lines,
but one of the movie's funniest moments doesn't

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:55.390
have any words at all. It comes at the very
end of the movie. As everyone celebrates,

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:00.139
Poe Dameron sees his old friend Zorii Bliss.
They lock eyes. Poe gives Zorii an inviting

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:04.600
tilt of his head. Zorii shakes him off. Poe
looks disappointed. The audience bursts into

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:05.160
laughter.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.260
The subtext should go right over kids' heads,
but every adult in the theater will realize

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:13.700
that Poe was asking Zorii if she wanted to
get busy. They'll also know that Zorii completely

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.340
shut him down. Oh well. There's no harm in
trying. Look, Poe just defeated an entire

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:23.040
fleet of Star Destroyers. He won the war.
Emotions are riding high. Who can blame him

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.300
for calling up an ex to blow off some steam?

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:30.560
Rey, Finn, and Poe's quest takes them to the
planet Pasaana, where a festival is taking

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:35.260
place. The party, C-3PO explains, is thrown
by the Pasaana's natives, the Aki-Aki, and

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:37.720
is held once every 42 years.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:41.519
If you're one of the lucky young'uns who grew
up in an age when new Star Wars movies have

00:03:41.519 --> 00:03:45.029
always been a thing, that number won't mean
anything to you. If you've been following

00:03:45.029 --> 00:03:49.400
the Skywalker Saga since the very beginning,
you should know immediately how Abrams and

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:55.370
his co-writer, Chris Terrio, landed on 42.
Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope came out

00:03:55.370 --> 00:04:00.820
in 1977. Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of
Skywalker came out in 2019. Guess how many

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:01.940
years apart that is.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:04.480
"42."

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.819
Maybe that's a clue for the future, too. Disney
says that its next Star Wars film will debut

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:18.060
in 2022, so you might as well go ahead and
set aside some time in 2064 now. You'll certainly

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.260
want to see how the next saga ends.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:25.120
The Rise of Skywalker reveals that before
he joined the Resistance, Poe Dameron used

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:29.570
to run spice. The way the other characters
react, it's not a good thing, but it doesn't

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:34.370
sound so bad. Who doesn't add a pinch of cumin
or paprika to their dishes while they cook?

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.400
Even in space, food should taste good.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:49.320
Except that's not the kind of spice they're
talking about. Just from the language used,

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.500
as well as the precedent set by Frank Herbert's
Dune, mature members of the audience who don't

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.940
already know will quickly figure out that
in Star Wars "spice" is basically slang for

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:58.520
drugs.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.880
"He who controls the spice controls the universe."

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:07.480
Poe Dameron wasn't helping people season their
meals. He was profiting off of other peoples'

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:08.020
addictions.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:12.590
In the Star Wars universe, the drug trade
is just as vicious and exploitative as it

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:17.070
is in real life. It's not a good thing for
someone like Poe to be involved in. Of course,

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:21.620
in his prime, the renowned scoundrel Han Solo
was known to smuggle spice, too. No wonder

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:22.180
Leia likes him.

